{
  "raw": {
    "https://www.employment.mtu.edu/en-us/job/494246/assistant-or-associate-professor-in-strategic-management": {
      "title": "Assistant or Associate Professor in Strategic  Management",
      "description": "Assistant or Associate Professor in Strategic Management Apply now Job No: 26152 Department: College of Business Work Type: Faculty Location: Main Campus (Houghton, MI) Full Time / Part Time: Full Time Categories: Business Applications Close: Applications received by November 1st will receive full consideration. Michigan Technological University is an R1 technological research university founded in 1885 in Houghton. Our rural campus is situated just miles from Lake Superior in Michigan's scenic Upper Peninsula and is home to nearly 7,500 students from more than 60 countries around the world. Consistently ranked among the best universities in the country for return on investment, Michigan’s flagship technological university offers more than 185 undergraduate and graduate degree programs. Research focus areas include defense, health, energy, automotive, environment, and aerospace. The area’s waters, forests, and snowfall support year-round recreation, including skiing, snowboarding, hiking, biking, and paddling. The University is an integral part of the region, supported by a friendly and welcoming community that takes pride in being a true college town. We embrace our size, climate, sense of adventure, and originality. Summary Michigan Technological University is seeking a Tenure-track faculty position in Management at the rank of Assistant or Associate Professor for our College of Business department, with an anticipated start date of Fall 2027. We seek candidates with demonstrated expertise in Strategy and Entrepreneurship and the ability to teach undergraduate and graduate courses in Strategic Management, Entrepreneurship, International Management, and other related areas consistent with the needs of the College. Applicants must have earned a doctoral degree in Management or a closely related discipline from an AACSB-accredited institution by the time of appointment. Candidates applying for the rank of Associate Professor must possess a record of scholarly achievement, including publications and other accomplishments in high-quality journals, that warrants appointment at the associate professor level. Responsibilities and Essential Duties • Develop and sustain a vigorous research program with national visibility. • Contribute effectively to undergraduate and graduate teaching through a student-centric, experiential approach in both the on-campus and online modalities. • Constructively and actively engage in service activities at the departmental, college, university, and professional levels. Required Education, Certifications, Licensures • PhD in Management from an AACSB-accredited school Required Experience • Evidence of research activity leading to publication of scholarly work in high-quality, peer-reviewed journals appropriate to the field of study commensurate with rank. • Evidence of the ability to independently teach management courses. Desirable Education and/or Experience • PhD in Strategic Management/International Management/ Entrepreneurship from an AACSB-accredited school. • Documented publications in high-quality, peer-reviewed journals in management commensurate with the rank. • Documented teaching experience in an institution of higher education with excellent teaching evaluations commensurate with the rank. • Documented industry experience. • Documented experience in securing research grants. • Documented service contributions at the college, university, or national level. • Evidence of serving as a committee member or chair of doctoral dissertations. Required Knowledge, Skills, and/or Abilities • Evidence of knowledge of the AACSB and its role in business colleges and schools • Demonstrated commitment to undergraduate and graduate teaching, program growth, and student success. • Demonstrated strong oral and written communication and presentation skills. Desirable Knowledge, Skills, and/or Abilities • The ability to contribute effectively to undergraduate and graduate teaching with a student-centric, learner-oriented, experiential approach to instruction in residential and online modalities. • Demonstrated ability to design and deliver an academic course in areas of expertise, in both on-campus and online formats. • Documented broad knowledge and skills across business disciplines. • Demonstrated success in, or potential future contributions to, working with people with a wide variety of backgrounds and viewpoints. Language, Mathematics and/or Reasoning Skills • Proficiency in English to teach and conduct research in English. Work Environment and/or Physical Demands WORK ENVIRONMENT: The work environment characteristics described here are representative of those an employee encounters while performing the essential functions of this job. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions. The noise level in the work environment is usually low to moderate. Required Training and Other Conditions of Employment Every employee at Michigan Technological University will receive the following 4 required trainings; additional training may be required by the department. Required University Training: • Employee Safety Overview • Anti-Harassment, Discrimination, Retaliation Training • Annual Data Security Training • Annual Title IX Training Background Check: Offers of employment are contingent upon and not considered finalized until the required background check has been performed and the results received and assessed. Full-Time Equivalent (FTE) % (1=100%) 1 FLSA Status Exempt Appointment Term 9 months Pay Rate/Salary The minimum salary for this position is 140,000. The final salary will depend on the rank, experience, and qualifications. Title of Position Supervisor Dean of College of Business Posting Type Internal & External Posting Dependent on Funding No To perform this job successfully, an individual must be able to perform each essential duty satisfactorily. The requirements listed are representative of the knowledge, skill, and/or ability required. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions. If you require any auxiliary aids, services, or accommodations during Michigan Tech’s hiring process please notify the Human Resources office at 906-487-2280 or hr-help@mtu.edu. Other Conditions of Employment: Please note that successful applicants are responsible for ensuring their eligibility to work in the United States (i.e. a citizen or national of the United States, a lawful permanent resident, a foreign national authorized to work in the United States without the need of an employer sponsorship) on or before the effective date of your appointment, and maintain eligibility without sponsorship throughout your appointment. Michigan Technological University is an Equal Opportunity Educational Institution/Equal Opportunity Employer that provides equal opportunity for all, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. The Annual Security and Fire Safety Report contains current campus safety and disciplinary policies, crime statistics for the previous 3 calendar years, and on-campus student housing fire safety policies and fire statistics for the previous 3 calendar years. Michigan Tech will provide a paper copy upon request; please contact the Michigan Tech Public Safety. In compliance with the federal Drug-Free Schools and Communities Act (DFSCA) and its implementing regulations (34 CFR Part 86), Michigan Tech is committed to maintaining a drugfree campus environment and actively promoting the health and safety of its community. Find our notice that outlines the University's policies, legal sanctions, health risks, and available support resources related to the unlawful possession, use, or distribution of illicit drugs and alcohol. Required Education, Certifications, Licensures* (minimum requirements) Advertised: 21 Sep 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications Close: Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://www.employment.mtu.edu/en-us/job/494265/assistant-teaching-professor-nursing": {
      "title": "Assistant Teaching Professor, Nursing",
      "description": "Assistant Teaching Professor, Nursing Apply now Job No: 26160 Department: School of Health, Human, & Bio Sys Work Type: Faculty Location: Main Campus (Houghton, MI) Full Time / Part Time: Full Time Categories: Nursing Applications Close: Ensured Consideration Date: November 1, 2026 Michigan Technological University is an R1 technological research university founded in 1885 in Houghton. Our rural campus is situated just miles from Lake Superior in Michigan's scenic Upper Peninsula and is home to nearly 7,500 students from more than 60 countries around the world. Consistently ranked among the best universities in the country for return on investment, Michigan’s flagship technological university offers more than 185 undergraduate and graduate degree programs. Research focus areas include defense, health, energy, automotive, environment, and aerospace. The area’s waters, forests, and snowfall support year-round recreation, including skiing, snowboarding, hiking, biking, and paddling. The University is an integral part of the region, supported by a friendly and welcoming community that takes pride in being a true college town. We embrace our size, climate, sense of adventure, and originality. Summary The Biological Sciences Program within the School of Health, Human, and Biological Systems at Michigan Technological University is seeking applications for an assistant/associate teaching professor. Primary consideration will be for applicants at the rank of Assistant Teaching Professor, although applicants with the experience and accomplishments commensurate with a higher rank may be considered for an appointment at the rank of Associate Teaching Professor. Instructional track faculty in Nursing are primarily responsible for the teaching and supervision of nursing students in the classroom, lab, and clinical settings. Primary teaching responsibilities will include the development and delivery of courses in the areas of Nursing Fundamentals, Maternal-Child Nursing, and Medical-Surgical Nursing or may be assigned based on need and as appropriate. Additional academic duties for all instructional-track faculty include participation in assessment activities and committee assignments. Responsibilities and Essential Duties 1. Instruction of classes, simulation, and clinical components as assigned. 2. Direct and indirect oversight of students in diverse clinical settings, including direct, individualized supervision of patient care, physical assessments, nursing interventions, and the administration of medications. 3. Coordination of clinical, lab, simulation and course assignments in collaboration with the faculty team within the academic level assigned. 4. Evaluation of students in class and clinical/lab settings. 5. Regular communication with students regarding progress. 6. Maintenance of student academic records. 7. Uphold expected course outcomes. 8. Participate in program assessment activities, committee assignments, and academic advising. 9. Uphold high standards in teaching, advising, and service responsibilities. 10. Advise, lead, supervise, motivate, and mentor students. 11. Perform various administrative duties as required or assigned. 12. Maintain and safeguard confi dential data under HIPAA and FERPA regulations. 13. Adhere to university policies and procedures and maintain faculty expectations as required by the university, Michigan Board of Nursing, and accreditation. 14. Maintain current clinical competency and knowledge. 15. Complete all campus and clinical site orientation and trainings. 16. Facilitate and/or conduct student orientation at clinical sites. 17. Be familiar with and comply with clinical site agency policies and procedures. 18. Work collegially and professionally with students, faculty, staff , and external constituents. 19. Perform other duties as assigned. Required Education, Certifications, Licensures Master’s Degree in nursing or related field with a Bachelor of Science degree in Nursing received from an accredited nursing program. Unrestricted license to practice as a Registered Nurse in the State of Michigan OR current state of residence with ability to obtain a Michigan Nursing license before hire. Current BLS certification Required Experience Minimum of 3 years of clinical nursing experience. Desirable Education and/or Experience Doctoral degree in nursing, education, or related field. Previous teaching experience in academic, clinical settings, and online. Maternal-newborn or pediatric experience. Broad clinical nursing experience. Required Knowledge, Skills, and/or Abilities Highly developed verbal and written communication skills and the ability to present eff ectively to small and large groups. Strong interpersonal skills and ability to work eff ectively at all levels in a collaborative team environment. Meet the physical demands of teaching in a clinical environment for extended periods. Proficient computer skills. Desirable Knowledge, Skills, and/or Abilities Demonstrated success in, or potential future contributions to, working with persons from diverse backgrounds, creating a sense of belonging, and fostering a fair, objective, welcoming place to work for persons with a wide variety of personal characteristics and viewpoints. Language, Mathematics and/or Reasoning Skills Apply critical thinking, clinical reasoning, and problem-solving to nursing education and clinical situations. Perform and teach mathematical calculations relevant to nursing practice. Read, interpret, and apply professional literature, clinical information, policies, regulations, and accreditation standards. Communicate clearly and professionally in written and verbal formats with students, colleagues, healthcare professionals, and community partners. Work Environment and/or Physical Demands The work environment is that of a typical offi ce and/or classroom/lab setting. The noise level in the work environment is usually low to moderate. Work will also be performed in a medical/clinical environment. Clinical and lab environments may involve exposure to operating circumstances that require following standard and prescribed safety precautions. Required Training and Other Conditions of Employment Every employee at Michigan Technological University will receive the following training courses: ● Employee Safety Overview ● Annual Data Security Training ● Anti-Harassment, Discrimination, Retaliation Training ● Annual Title IX Training Additional training will be required by the department on a periodic basis. Background Check: Offers of employment are contingent upon and not considered fi nalized until the required background check has been performed and the results received and assessed. Other Conditions of Employment: The successful applicant will be responsible for ensuring eligibility for employment in the United States on or before the eff ective date of the appointment. This is not an E-Verified Position. Full-Time Equivalent (FTE) % (1=100%) 1 FLSA Status Exempt Appointment Term 9 months Shift Pay Rate/Salary Title of Position Supervisor Teaching Professor, Director Posting Type Internal and External Posting Dependent on Funding No Special Instructions to Applicants (if applicable) The ideal starting date is Spring 2027. Review of applications will begin on November 02, 2026 and applications should arrive by that date for maximal consideration. However, late applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Applicants will need to provide a letter of application describing qualifications for and interest in the position, a resume or curriculum vitae, teaching philosophy, and nursing license. Applicants will also be asked for the names and contact information for three reference providers. Additional Information To perform this job successfully, an individual must be able to perform each essential duty satisfactorily. The requirements listed are representative of the knowledge, skill, and/or ability required. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions. If you require any auxiliary aids, services, or accommodations during Michigan Tech’s hiring process please notify the Human Resources office at 906-487-2280 or hr-help@mtu.edu. Other Conditions of Employment: Please note that successful applicants are responsible for ensuring their eligibility to work in the United States (i.e. a citizen or national of the United States, a lawful permanent resident, a foreign national authorized to work in the United States without the need of an employer sponsorship) on or before the effective date of your appointment, and maintain eligibility without sponsorship throughout your appointment. Michigan Technological University is an Equal Opportunity Educational Institution/Equal Opportunity Employer that provides equal opportunity for all, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. The Annual Security and Fire Safety Report contains current campus safety and disciplinary policies, crime statistics for the previous 3 calendar years, and on-campus student housing fire safety policies and fire statistics for the previous 3 calendar years. Michigan Tech will provide a paper copy upon request; please contact the Michigan Tech Public Safety. In compliance with the federal Drug-Free Schools and Communities Act (DFSCA) and its implementing regulations (34 CFR Part 86), Michigan Tech is committed to maintaining a drugfree campus environment and actively promoting the health and safety of its community. Find our notice that outlines the University's policies, legal sanctions, health risks, and available support resources related to the unlawful possession, use, or distribution of illicit drugs and alcohol. Required Education, Certifications, Licensures* (minimum requirements) Advertised: 16 Oct 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications Close: Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email